ED_DATE x 3 5cm and is located in the lateral half of the specimen  and an additional REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm area in the medial aspect of the specimen  No prior biopsy site or discrete masses are identified in this specimen  Representative sections of fibrous tissue are submitted from lateral to medial in cassettes C L with cassettes G and H corresponding to tissue from the center of the specimen  No lymph nodes are identified within the specimen  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm left mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 8 4cm unremarkable skin ellipse on the anterior surface of the specimen with a 3 0cm in diameter areola with a 1 2cm in diameter x 0 5cm in nipple which is grossly unremarkable  There is a stitch in the superior or 12 o clock aspect of the specimen as per the surgeons  note on the requisition form  The anterior resection margin is blue inked and the posterior resection margin is black inked  The specimen is sectioned along the supero inferior access from medial to lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan pink mass located in the upper outer quadrant of the specimen  The remainder of the specimen consists of adipose tissue with firm tan fibrotic areas throughout  Throughout the fibrous tissue as far as 7 0cm away from the main mass there are numerous   REMOVED_DATE to 0 2cm in diameter tan pink nodule  The main mass is REMOVED_DATE to 0 2cm away from the closest resection margin which is the posterior margin 3 5cm away from the lateral edge of the specimen and 4 5cm from the superior aspect of the specimen  Two nodular soft tissue fragments are disected as the lateral aspect of the specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  Representative sections are submitted as follows  M  Unremarkable medial breast tissue  N S  Fibrous tissue with pink nodules  submitted fro