Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  18 MAY 96 ACCESSIONED ON  18 MAY 96 at 11 46 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM  WITH LYMPHATIC VASCULAR INVASION  SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  ADMIXED WITH AND ADJACENT TO INVASIVE COMPONENT  NOTE  Invasive tumor extends to within 0 2cm of the nearest  superior  margin  Definite blood vascular invasion is not identified  BREAST  RIGHT SUPERIOR MARGIN   FOCAL ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD Signed On  22 MAY 96 at 15 55                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  24 MAY 96 at 09 12 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  in two parts  Designated  right breast  is an oriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm breast fragment  inked black  with anterior superior surface overinked blue and anterior inferior surface overinked green  Sectioned to show an approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm stellate  firm  white mass within 0 3cm of the superior surface  Representative sections submitted from lateral to medial in cassettes A K  with entire mass included  Designated  superior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm breast fragment containing a short suture designating the superior aspect  The long suture  to designate the posterior deep margin  has been previously separated from the specimen  One surface of the breast fragment is flat  and the other is curved with lobulated fat  The curved surface is overinked blue in the superior region and green in the inferior region  The parenchyma is unremarkable  and representative sections are submitted from one end to the other in L T  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  William E Butler  M D  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  Irene Kuter  M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST PART B  SUPERIOR MARGIN   report_end  , Absent.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  11 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 19 13 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 2 3   EXTENDING TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE INKED DEEP RESECTION MARGIN  AND WITH BLOOD VASCULAR  VENOUS  INVASION   SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  INTERMEDIATE TO HIGH PRESENT IN 5 OF 5 SLIDES  EXTENDING TO THE INKED DEEP RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE   3  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 20 OF 20 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  NOTE  Several foci are highly suspicious for lymphatic invasion  Dr  Koerner agrees with the interpretation of blood vascular invasion  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 18 12                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 21 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast and axillary dissection  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm mastectomy with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm skin ellipse with an unremarkable 1 5cm nipple  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm axillary tail is attached to the main specimen  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm firm  tan white stellate nodule extending to approximately REMOVED_DATE to 0 2cm of the deep resection margin  Further sectioning reveals the remainder of the breast to be composed of predominantly fibrous  tan rubbery tissue intermixed with unremarkable adipose tissue  A representative section of the firm mass and deep resection margin is submitted in cassette A  Representative sections of the remainder of the mass are submitted in cassettes B through E  Representative sections of unremarkable parenchyma are submitted entirely in cassette F  The axillary tail is sectioned to reveal multiple rubbery tan pink lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 2 0cm  The lymph nodes are submitted entirely in cassettes G through M  The nipple is trisected and submitted entirely in cassette N  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  AMBULATORY GEN SURG   ACC 457 REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT  and AXILLARY CONTENTS   report_end  , Absent.
