 1 0cm from the inferior margin  It is more than 2cm from both the medial and the lateral resection margins  There is a 0 3cm S shaped clip in one of the sections  Section Code   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Section of the area containing the clip towards the anterior and inferior resection margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Section containing the clip towards the superior resection margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrous area towards the posterior section margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrous area towards the superior section margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrous area towards the anterior section margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Area away from the main lesion containing a potential calcified vessel   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral resection margin en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial resection margin en face  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast axillary node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue  Potential lymph nodes are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One potential lymph node  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Five potential lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Five potential lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Six potential lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Six potential lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Four potential lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three potential lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three potential lymph nodes  Gross Dictation by Aleksandr Vasilyev M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Aleksandr Vasilyev M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Aleksandr Vasilyev M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Aleksandr Vasilyev M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   DISSECTION , Absent.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 MEEI MRN  REMOVED_DATE Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D  Resident  Maylee Hsu  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D  CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 48 year old woman with a history of left breast cancer who is status post neoadjuvant chemotherapy  She also has irregular bleeding  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  1  INVASIVE ADENOCARCINOMA OF THE BREAST  see Table  1 and note   2  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA TUMOR SIZE  At least 1 7cm  measured microscopically   The tumor is diffusely infiltrative  and is present in multiple microscopic foci and as numerous isolated cells and a few small clusters  The tumor cells are present in a stellate area of dense fibrosis measuring at least 1 7cm  The morphology is compatible with the patient s history of ductal carcinoma  The presence of only rare isolated cells in a zone of dense fibrosis likely reflects prior neoadjuvant therapy  GRADE  The tumor is too small to accurately grade  LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  Invasive carcinoma extends to less than 0 1cm from the lateral margin of the specimen along a broad front  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  See prior report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA CONTENTS   DISSECTION    ISOLATED TUMOR CELLS PRESENT IN 2 OF 10 LYMPH NODES  2 10     HEALING BIOPSY SITE  TABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS  2 SUMMARY OF AXILLARY LYMPH NODES TOTAL NUMBER OF POSITIVE LYMPH NODES  2  TOTAL NUMBER OF LYMPH NODES EXAMINED  10  Number of lymph nodes with metastases 0 02cm or less  isolated tumor cells   2  Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 02cm to 0 2cm  micrometastases   0  Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 2cm  macrometastases   0  Extracapsular extension  None  Other forms of axillary involvement  None  ENDOMETRIUM  CURETTAGE    FRAGMENT OF INACTIVE ENDOMETRIUM  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left breast lumpectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm fibrofatty soft tissue fragment with a localization needle in place and short stitch marking the superior margin and a long stitch marking the lateral margin  The specimen is orientated along the superior inferior axis and inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  lateral yellow  and medial green  On sectioning there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm firm ill defined mass located  0 3cm from the black inked posterior margin  0 5cm from the yellow inked lateral and green inked medial margin  1 0cm from the superior margin  and 0 8cm from the inferior margin  Representative sections are taken as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   superior tip  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   inferior tip  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   representative sections of the mass  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   representative section away from mass Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm fibrofatty soft tissue fragment with multiple possible lymph nodes dissected out  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Multiple lymph nodes with one possible lymph node bisected in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  EMC   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm aggregate of soft tissue fragment  submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA CONTENTS   DISSECTION PART C  ENDOMETRIUM  CURETTAGE  report_end  , Absent.
